{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K1ZX2w5Sj8nRfPEfKgQwCG","type":"tool_result","content":"# Plan for #386\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Steps\n\nDesign anchors found in the code: part 2 (#385) left `closeout.Deps.Network` unset in `internal/servecmd/reaping.go` (`wiring.closer`); `closeout.Job.Network *NetworkState` and `NetworkRounds` already exist in `internal/closeout/network.go`; the pure `closeout.Build` (`internal/closeout/plan.go`) makes the triage `done` plan in its `default:` branch; `Prepare` (`internal/closeout/prepare.go`) is where state is read and persisted into the Record, so `Build` stays pure and `ResumeJob` replays the stored Plan.\n\n1. **Round state types** (`internal/closeout/network.go`, new symbols). Extend `NetworkState` (zero-value compatible, `json:\",omitempty\"`, no `recordVersion` bump; add the new fields to the recordVersion comment in `closeout.go`):\n   - `Round bool`: a network round is open, meaning the newest closed worker close-out of the issue has `Plan.Bounced` and no triage-engineer `done` close-out has closed after it.\n   - `Done []string`: the other triage roles (not `lead`, not `engineer`) that finished `done` before; computed in `Prepare` from the issue's triage close-outs.\n   Add `func NetworkRoundOpen(ctx, s closeoutsOf, issue int) (open bool, doneRoles []string, err error)` (new) reading `CloseoutsOf(issue, \"triage\")` and `\"worker\"` records via `decode`. \"Consumed\" is stored in the engineer's own Plan (step 3), so a later human re-request of the engineer sees no open round and does not re-arm.\n2. **Plan fields** (`internal/closeout/plan.go`). Add to `Plan`: `Rearmed bool` (`json:\",omitempty\"`), `Rerun []string` (`json:\",omitempty\"`; roles whose `:done` the lead must remove, persisted), and `Inputs []Input` (see step 4). Add `type Input struct{ Path, Provider, URL string }` (new).\n3. **Lead re-arm in `Build`** (`internal/closeout/plan.go`, `default:` branch, pure). When `j.Stage == StageTriage && j.Role == \"engineer\" && j.Network != nil && j.Network.Round`: set `p.Rearmed = true`, `p.Rerun = j.Network.Done`, and put into `p.Requests` the label `ard:pending` (`labels.Pending`) and into `p.Remove` `labels.Done(StageTriage, \"lead\")`, ordered before the engineer's own `:done` terminal label (check how `finish`/`request` in `closeout.go` order Requests, Remove and Terminal; Requests are applied in the request phase before Terminal, and the \"remove X before :done\" ordering for the bounce in part 2 shows removals precede it, so confirm `finish`'s order and add a test pinning it). In the lead's close-out (`j.Role == \"lead\"`), when `j.Network != nil && len(j.Network.Rerun) > 0`, append `Label{n, labels.Request(StageTriage, r)}` for each persisted role and `Label{n, labels.Done(StageTriage, r)}` removals for the same roles in the request phase, so the lead's request phase removes `:done` before the others run. Add `Rerun []string` to `NetworkState` for this (the lead job reads it from the same persisted round). Also make sure `:done` removal of an absent label is tolerated like `p.Bounced` does in `finish` (the `ErrNotFound` skip): extend that condition to `p.Rearmed || len(p.Rerun) > 0`.\n4. **`inputs:` frontmatter** (`internal/closeout/rolefile.go`). Add `Inputs *[]rawInput \\`yaml:\"inputs\"\\`` to the raw struct (the known-keys list, strict decode like `fetched`), `RoleFile.Inputs []Input`, a validator `inputsOf` (new) modelled on `fetchedOf`: max 10 entries (`MaxInputs`), each `path` required, `provider` one of `human` or `worker` (document in proposal), `url` https-only with the same checks as `networkOf` (`MaxNetworkURL`). Allowed on triage `engineer` only (reject on other roles, as `fetched` is rejected on non-workers around line 299). Cleaning `path` here: reject with a `malformed(...)` error; the gate re-checks (step 6) because the Plan is the only trusted copy. Copy `rf.Inputs` into `p.Inputs` in `Build`.\n5. **`Prepare` computes and persists the round** (`internal/closeout/prepare.go`, next to the part 2 block). For `j.Stage == StageTriage && d.Network != nil`: call `NetworkRoundOpen`; when the job is the engineer and rf.Status is `done`, set `j.Network = &NetworkState{Round: open, Done: doneRoles}`; when the job is the lead and a round is open (a bounce record newer than the engineer's last `done`, and the lead's Plan `Rearmed` was set by the engineer), set `j.Network = &NetworkState{Round: true, Rerun: <engineer plan's Rerun>}`. Keep part 2's worker branch unchanged. Because `Prepare` stores the resulting `Plan` in the Record before any label is applied, `ResumeJob` replays it without recomputing.\n6. **Gate reads inputs from main** (`internal/triage/fanin.go`, `internal/triage/loop.go`, `internal/servecmd/triage.go`).\n   - New `Deps.MainFile func(ctx context.Context, path string, max int64) (data []byte, sha string, ok bool, err error)` (new field in `triage.Deps`), implemented in `servecmd/triage.go` next to `planExists` by fetching `+refs/heads/main:`+`planRef`, `g.RevParse(planRef)` for the SHA, then `g.FileAt`. Reuse `planExists`'s fetch so there is one fetch per tick.\n   - New pure `func cleanInputPath(p string) error` in `fanin.go`: `path.Clean(p) == p`, not absolute, no `..`, not under `.ard/`, `.github/` or `.git` (including `.git`-prefixed names such as `.gitmodules`? reject exactly `.git` and `.git/`), length cap 200, no NUL or backslash.\n   - New `inputCache` in `tick` or `Loop` (a `map[sha]map[path]bool` guarded by a mutex): `exists(sha, path)` reads through `MainFile` once per SHA. Size cap: a file larger than `closeout.MaxRoleFileBytes`-style constant `maxInputBytes` (new, 50 MiB) counts as an error: `needs-human`.\n   - New `decideInputs(inputs []closeout.Input, workers map[string]config.Role, exists func(path string) bool) inputsResult` (pure): bad path → `fHuman` reason `bad-input-path`; provider `worker` and the chosen worker role has `network: false` → `fHuman` reason `worker-no-network`; provider `human` and the file missing on main → new verdict `fWaitInputs` with the missing list. Add `rInputsMissing = \"inputs-missing\"`, `rBadInput`, `rNoNetwork` reasons and a `gateHuman` case each (fixed text, never issue text).\n   - The engineer's `Plan.Inputs` come from the lead's close-out store: add `closeout.InputsOf(ctx, s, issue) ([]Input, bool, error)` (new, like `LeadWorker`) returning the newest closed triage-engineer record's `Plan.Inputs`; call it in `gateIssue` when a network round is open.\n   - The waiting comment (marker `<!-- ard:triage gate=inputs round=<n> -->` via `postOnce`) lists each missing path and the capture-note format (the `CAPTURE.md` table described in proposal \"Fetched inputs\"). The status issue (`internal/controller` status rendering, found via `servecmd/digest.go` `StatusIssue`) shows \"waiting for inputs\": add a small counter exported from the triage loop, reported like the other loop state; locate the existing renderer first and keep it minimal.\n7. **Approval per round** (`internal/triage/fanin.go`). In `gateReady`, change `if t.cfg.RequireApproval` to `if t.cfg.RequireApproval || networkRound`, where `networkRound` comes from `closeout.NetworkRounds`-style detection (a closed worker close-out with `Plan.Bounced` exists): add `closeout.NetworkRoundCount(ctx, s, issue) (int, error)` reusing `NetworkRounds`' decode loop. It is true even when the engineer removed every network need and `require_approval: false`. Add a `round int` parameter to `approved` and `askApproval`; the marker becomes `<!-- ard:triage gate=approval job=<id> round=<n> -->` only when `round > 0` (round 0 keeps the old marker, so existing issues are unaffected). The existing staleness check (`approval` event must be after `lastTriageDone`) already ignores an older approval, because the re-run triage adds new `:done` labels after it; keep that and add a test.\n8. **Switch the bounce on** (`internal/servecmd/reaping.go`). Replace the \"deliberately unset\" comment and pass `Network: w.Store` in `closeout.Deps`. `*state.Store` already has `CloseoutsOf`; confirm with a compile.\n9. **Engineer prompt starter** (`internal/roles/triage/engineer/prompt.txt`): document the `inputs:` frontmatter key (`path`, `provider`, `url`), and keep `internal/roles/network_prompts_test.go` passing. The live copy `.ard/triage/engineer/` is a protected path; do not edit it (see Risk).\n10. **Docs** (`docs/proposal.md`): extend the \"Network needs (#384)\" paragraph with the re-arm, persisted round state, `inputs:` gate, per-round approval marker and that the bounce is now on; update the label state machine table/notes and the Configuration paragraph only if the code adds a setting (this plan adds none). Run `go test ./internal/docscheck/...` if the repository checks docs.\n\n### Test plan\n\nCommand: `make lint test` (`go test ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `gofmt -l .`). Targeted: `go test ./internal/closeout ./internal/triage ./internal/servecmd ./internal/roles`.\n\n- `internal/closeout/network_test.go`:\n  - `TestEngineerDoneRearmsLead`: engineer `done`, `Network{Round:true, Done:[security]}` → Requests contain `ard:pending`, Remove contains `ard:triage:lead:done` before `ard:triage:engineer:done` is applied; `Rearmed` true.\n  - `TestEngineerDoneNoRound`: `Network` nil or `Round:false` (human re-request) → no `ard:pending`, no removals.\n  - `TestLeadCloseoutReopensRoles`: lead job with `Rerun:[security,docs]` → request labels added and `:done` removed for both; the lead's own `:done` last.\n  - `TestPrepareRoundOpen`: store with a closed bounced worker record and no engineer done after it → `Round:true` and `Done` equals the other roles that ran `done`; after the first engineer `done` is closed, `NetworkRoundOpen` is false.\n  - `TestResumeReplaysRound`: save the Record after `Prepare`, change the store so the round would compute differently, `ResumeJob` → label calls match the persisted plan.\n  - `TestRolefileInputs`: valid list parses; bad provider, non-https url, unknown key, more than 10 entries, `inputs` on a non-engineer role → malformed. Old record JSON without the new fields decodes as before.\n- `internal/triage/fanin_test.go`:\n  - `TestCleanInputPath`: table of `a/b.txt` ok; `/abs`, `../x`, `a/../b`, `./a`, `.ard/x`, `.github/w.yml`, `.git/config`, `a\\\\b`, empty, over-long → error.\n  - `TestGateHoldsForHumanInput`: human input missing on main → waiting comment lists each missing path plus the capture-note format; no worker label; posted once across ticks.\n  - `TestGateInputsPresent`: input on main → continues to approval, posts \"ready for approval\" with the round marker; `MainFile` called once per SHA (cache), again on a new SHA.\n  - `TestGateWorkerInputNoNetwork`: provider `worker` with a `network: false` worker → `needs-human`, fixed text.\n  - `TestGateBadPath`: bad path → `needs-human`, nothing read from main.\n  - `TestNetworkRoundAlwaysNeedsApproval`: `RequireApproval=false` plus a bounced round, and an engineer plan with no inputs → still asks approval; a non-network issue with `RequireApproval=false` still starts the worker without approval.\n  - `TestApprovalMarkerPerRound`: an approval label applied before the re-run's `:done` is ignored and a fresh \"ready for approval\" with the round marker is posted; round 0 keeps the old marker.\n  - Re-run list: `TestRerunBeforeGate`: lead `:done` removed and `ard:pending` present → `decideFanIn` skips (`lead-requested`); after the lead and each re-opened role finish, the gate proceeds.\n- `internal/servecmd`: `TestCloserHasNetwork` (the Closer's `Deps.Network` is set); the existing triage e2e test gets one bounce-and-return scenario if it can run offline.\n- Edge cases: engineer `done` with `Network.Done` empty; the issue has no other triage roles; a second network round still ends `needs-human` (part 2 guard unchanged); `ErrNotFound` on removing an already-absent `:done`; `MainFile` error leaves the